  "title": "Global Integration of Technology and Space for National Geopolitical Advancement, Kerala's Strong Opposition to Mining Amendment Bill, India and Mauritius Sign Fuel Supply Agreement",
  "summary": "Union Minister Gajendra Shekhawat emphasized the convergence of space technology, AI, and other cutting-edge innovations to shape India's geopolitical future. Kerala Chief Minister V.D. Satheesan opposes the Mines and Minerals (Development and Regulation) Amendment Bill, citing its potential violation of federal principles and the threat to state sovereignty over land. The Indian government faces opposition to a mega-infrastructure project on Great Nicobar Island, citing ecological and environmental concerns. India and Mauritius sign a five-year agreement to supply fuel for India’s needs.",
